@baseUrl = http://localhost:5207
@receptionistId = 1
@securityId = 2
@adminId = 3

### ---------------------------------
### Users / Actors Setup
### ---------------------------------
### NOTE:
### The current backend requires user IDs in visit actions:
### - checkedInById      (required at registration - POST /api/visits)
### - checkedOutById     (required at checkout)
### - changedByUserId    (required for notify-host / host-acknowledge / deny /
###                        mark-attended / host-complete / close / cancel)
### But there are NO /api/users endpoints implemented yet.
### So these IDs must already exist in the database.
### Expected mock/demo IDs used by the frontend and HTTP file:
### - Receptionist -> 1
### - Security     -> 2
### - Admin        -> 3
###
### If your DB does not contain these users, visit registration/status actions will fail.
### Once UsersController exists, replace this section with real POST /api/users calls.

### Users - Expected demo actor ids
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/visits
Accept: application/json

### ---------------------------------
### Visitors
### ---------------------------------
### IdentificationType legend: 1=NationalId 2=Passport 3=DriverLicense 4=Other

### Visitors - Get all
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors
Accept: application/json

###

### Visitors - Get by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Visitors - Get all visits for one visitor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors/1/visits
Accept: application/json

###

### Visitors - Create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Jane Visitor",
  "phoneNumber": "0799993999",
  "email": "jane.visitor@example.com",
  "identificationType": 1,
  "identificationNumber": "NIDA-123456782",
  "organization": "Acme Logistics",
  "photoUrl": "https://example.com/photos/jane-visitor.jpg"
}

###

### Visitors - Update
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors/1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Jane Visitor Updated",
  "phoneNumber": "0788888888",
  "email": "jane.visitor@example.com",
  "identificationType": 1,
  "identificationNumber": "NIDA-987654321",
  "organization": "Acme Logistics",
  "photoUrl": "https://example.com/photos/jane-visitor-updated.jpg",
  "isActive": true
}

###

### Visitors - Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/visitors/1
Accept: application/json

